{"duration_api_ms":206859,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"1a28a9ea-e8ba-4ba4-8b55-ede9ffad62f3","total_cost_usd":1.3393650000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":91903,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":16813,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":10538},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":91903,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":16813,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":91903,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":91903},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":16813,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":91903,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.3393650000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":10538,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-4-8","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"tool_name\":\"final\",\"arguments_json\":\"{\\\"response\\\":\\\"contract_version: 0.1.0\\\\nartifact_version: 1\\\\nwork_item: 20260908T113253\\\\nobservable_behaviour:\\\\n  - id: readme-reflects-provider\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"README.md names `claude_account` (Claude CLI, subscription OAuth, model `claude-sonnet-4-6`) as the default provider per ADR-019 and `anthropic_sdk` as an explicit, potentially-metered opt-in; no statement claims the Anthropic SDK is the default and nothing leads with a stale provider/auth description drawn from architecture.md §8/§9.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: readme-reflects-pipeline\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"README.md summarises the implemented M1–M5 pipeline status honestly: the server layer is carried but unwired (O-2) and forecasting (VC-POC-14) is registered-but-gated (O-4), not part of MVP.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: runbook-reflects-stages\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"RUNBOOK.md names, in current terms, the deterministic PR-gate tier (pytest, zero network), the manual/nightly live tier (`python -m evals.live`) reporting pass@k and pass^k separately, the `--pressure` probe whose transcripts a human must read, the three demo modes and banner semantics, and the provider override (`HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk`, potentially metered).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: release-note-present\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"Exactly one new releases/_next/<slug>.md exists carrying a `**Type:**` line and the mandatory `## Local deployment`, `## Manual steps` and `## Verification` (with a fenced bash block) sections, so the release-notes CI gate accepts the change; VERSION is untouched and no releases/v*.md is added.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: no-behaviour-change\\\\n    behaviour: \\\\\\\"run.py and demo.py change only help text, argparse `description`/`help=` and docstrings/comments where they name provider/model or eval stages; no runtime logic, exit code, control-flow or symbol behaviour changes.\\\\\\\"\\\\nrequired_outputs:\\\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    path: README.md\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"The primary lagging surface: its top-level provider/model, evaluation-tier and pipeline-status prose must be reconciled to ADR-019, O-2 and O-4.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    path: RUNBOOK.md\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"The request names runbook guidance as a reconciliation target; operator prose for auth, the two eval tiers, --pressure, demo modes, provider override and the pin/checkpoint rules must be confirmed/tightened in current terms.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    path: releases/_next/reconcile-doc-surfaces.md\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"The release-notes CI gate (.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml release-notes job + .claude/hooks/require-release-notes.sh) requires exactly one new releases/_next/*.md with a Type line and the mandatory sections; the PR is blocked without it. Executor must use this slug.\\\\\\\"\\\\npermitted_files:\\\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    path: run.py\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Help/description/docstring may be edited where it names provider/model or eval stages; contingent and no-logic per the plan. Editing it makes the change span a behaviour path (see decision-release-note-type).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    path: demo.py\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Mode/help/docstring prose may be aligned to ADR-017's three modes and banner semantics; contingent and no-logic. Must not add a `def render_*` or a second verbosity control (test_demo.py).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    path: tests/unit/test_run_cli.py\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Enforcing file over run.py: it greps run.py source and asserts the require_credentials message strings. Editable only if a require_credentials message string is deliberately changed, in which case its paired assertions must move in lockstep.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    path: tests/unit/test_demo.py\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Enforcing file over demo.py: it asserts ADR-017 properties (no `def render_*`, renders through cli.render_text, GROUPS/GATED partition, single LOG_LEVEL setdefault, no setLevel) and may gain/adjust an assertion over edited mode/help text.\\\\\\\"\\\\ndeterministic:\\\\n  - id: full-test-suite\\\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    command: \\\\\\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"The declared verification suite (manifest k-12Harness.verify) exits zero with no failures and no errors; pre-existing xfail/xpass are unaffected.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expect:\\\\n      exit_code: 0\\\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\\\n  - id: demo-properties-green\\\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    command: \\\\\\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_demo.py -q\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"The ADR-017 property tests over demo.py stay green after the help/docstring edits (no def render_*, renders through run.py, groups partition, single verbosity control).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expect:\\\\n      exit_code: 0\\\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\\\n  - id: run-cli-green\\\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    command: \\\\\\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_run_cli.py -q\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"The CLI tests, including the require_credentials message and default_credentials source assertions, stay green after any run.py help edits.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expect:\\\\n      exit_code: 0\\\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\\\n  - id: contract-pin-unchanged\\\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    command: \\\\\\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py -q\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"The contract pin test stays green, proving no accidental contract/PINNED.json or CONTRACT_VERSION change (ADR-008); this is a docs-only WI with no contract bump.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expect:\\\\n      exit_code: 0\\\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\\\n  - id: release-note-typed\\\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\\\n    command: \\\\\\\"grep -RE '^\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\*Type:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\* (patch|minor|major)' releases/_next/\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"The added releases/_next/ note declares a patch|minor|major Type line, as the release-notes gate requires; the base commit carries only releases/_next/.gitkeep, so exit 0 here depends on the change.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expect:\\\\n      exit_code: 0\\\\nmust_not_change:\\\\n  - invariant: \\\\\\\"The require_credentials message strings in run.py asserted by tests/unit/test_run_cli.py (`claude setup-token`, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, and the `default_credentials` source reference) — kept intact, or their paired assertions updated in the same change.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - invariant: \\\\\\\"ADR-017 properties of demo.py: no `def render_*`, every answer renders via `cli.render_text(output)`, `demo.GROUPS`/`demo.GATED` partition the registry, and the single `os.environ.setdefault(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"LOG_LEVEL\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", ...)` control point with no direct `setLevel` (tests/unit/test_demo.py).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - invariant: \\\\\\\"Runtime behaviour of run.py and demo.py: no logic, exit code, argument parsing semantics or symbol behaviour change — only help/description/docstring/comment prose.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - invariant: \\\\\\\"contract/PINNED.json, tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py and settings.CONTRACT_VERSION: no contract version bump or re-pin in this WI.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - invariant: \\\\\\\"VERSION is not touched and no releases/v*.md is added (the release-notes gate refuses both); exactly one releases/_next/*.md is added.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - invariant: \\\\\\\"docs/architecture.md and docs/decisions.md (the pinned authority) are not edited; config/settings.py and the provider adapters (harness/claude_account_cli.py, harness/agent.py) carry no change.\\\\\\\"\\\\nfailure_behaviour:\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"A require_credentials message string in run.py is changed without updating tests/unit/test_run_cli.py.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"test_run_cli.py fails; the executor must either keep the message strings intact or update the paired assertions in the same change.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"demo.py grows a `def render_*`, stops rendering through `cli.render_text`, or adds a second verbosity control.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"tests/unit/test_demo.py fails; the demo must continue to render through run.py and keep the single LOG_LEVEL control.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - condition: \\\\\\\"VERSION is bumped, a releases/v*.md is added, no releases/_next/*.md is added, more than one is added, or the note lacks the Type line or a mandatory section.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    expected: \\\\\\\"The release-notes CI gate and the local require-release-notes.sh hook deny the PR with an actionable reason; the change is blocked until the note conforms.\\\\\\\"\\\\ncompatibility:\\\\n  - obligation: \\\\\\\"ADR-019: `claude_account` (Claude CLI, subscription OAuth, `claude-sonnet-4-6`) is the default provider and `anthropic_sdk` is explicit-and-potentially-metered; ADR-018 (Codex account) remains as history, superseded by ADR-019 — doc prose must state this and add no new superseding ADR.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - obligation: \\\\\\\"ADR-007: the live tier stays manual/nightly and never becomes a PR gate; the deterministic tier gates every PR at zero network cost.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - obligation: \\\\\\\"ADR-017: the demo has exactly three modes each announced by a tested banner and renders only through the product; doc prose must not contradict this.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - obligation: \\\\\\\"ADR-008 / ADR-015-3: the contract is pinned by hash and a bump is the loud four-step operation (re-pin, regenerate the prompt, regenerate the fixture bundle, re-point cases); the Anthropic SDK is pinned exactly alongside the framework as one compatibility surface — documented, not performed here.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - obligation: \\\\\\\"ADR-006: per-model cache minimums (CACHE_MIN_TOKENS) are re-verified on model upgrades and the cache regression check remains `cache_read_tokens > 0`.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - obligation: \\\\\\\"README.md's own precedence rule stands: docs/decisions.md is the source of truth on any conflict, so where architecture.md §8/§9 disagree with ADR-019 the surfaces adopt ADR-019.\\\\\\\"\\\\ncompatibility_baselines: []\\\\ncontract_requirements:\\\\n  - id: scope-is-the-file-list\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"The permitted change set is exactly required_outputs plus permitted_files. docs/architecture.md, docs/decisions.md, config/settings.py, the provider adapters, contract/PINNED.json, tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py, tests/unit/test_usage.py and harness/usage.py are outside scope.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: decision-checkpoint-referent\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"DECISION: which 'checkpoint compatibility rules' referent the doc surfaces reconcile to. Options: (a) the model-checkpoint/resume rule — the pinned account model (config/settings.py CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL) cannot resume a checkpoint produced by another model, per-model cache minimums re-verified on upgrade (ADR-006); (b) the eval-resume checkpoint (RUNBOOK §1 `--resume`); (c) the contract hash pin (ADR-008); (d) the SDK+framework pin surface (ADR-015-3). Neither Definition Pack reference defines a 'checkpoint' concept, so this is an owner choice. The rest of the contract is written on option (a). Affects: semantic checkpoint-rule-documented, observable_behaviour runbook-reflects-stages, and RUNBOOK.md / README.md content in required_outputs.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: decision-release-note-type\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"DECISION: whether the reconciliation edits the code entry points (run.py, demo.py) at all. Under the v1.2.0 path classes, any change to a root *.py behaviour path makes the release note `**Type:** minor`; a docs-only change (README, RUNBOOK, the note) is `**Type:** patch`. Options: (a) edit run.py/demo.py help/docstrings where they name provider/model/eval stages — release note Type: minor, run.py and demo.py are in the change set; (b) leave run.py/demo.py untouched — release note Type: patch. The contract is written on option (a) (the plan lists run.py/demo.py as in-scope surfaces) but keeps them in permitted_files so option (b) needs no restructuring; the release-note-typed deterministic accepts either Type. Affects: permitted_files (run.py, demo.py), observable_behaviour no-behaviour-change, semantic release-note-type-correct, deterministic release-note-typed.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: gap-architecture-adr-conflict\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"GAP: docs/architecture.md §8 (names the model plainly) and §9 (API-key/account-bearer auth) predate and conflict with docs/decisions.md ADR-018/019. Resolved by the repository's stated precedence (README.md: decisions.md is source of truth on any conflict): the surfaces adopt ADR-019; architecture.md is not edited here (its internal drift is out of scope).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: assumption-readme-primary\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"ASSUMPTION: README.md is the primary lagging surface; run.py, demo.py and RUNBOOK.md already largely reflect ADR-019, so reconciliation there is confirmation/tightening. The executor should diff each surface against the two pinned ADR sets before editing.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: assumption-model-literal-source\\\\n    requirement: \\\\\\\"ASSUMPTION: the implemented pipeline/provider reality lives partly in code the manifest did not pin (config/settings.py, run.py, harness/claude_account_cli.py); where prose must name the pinned model it should point at config/settings.py as the single source of truth rather than restating a literal that can drift.\\\\\\\"\\\\nsemantic:\\\\n  - id: provider-default-adopts-adr019\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"README.md and RUNBOOK.md describe `claude_account` (Claude CLI, subscription OAuth, `claude-sonnet-4-6`) as the default provider and `anthropic_sdk` as explicit/potentially-metered, with no residual claim that the Anthropic SDK is the default and no stale auth description contradicting ADR-019.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: pipeline-status-honest\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"README.md's pipeline summary states the M1–M5 reality without overstating it: the server layer is carried but unwired (O-2) and forecasting is registered-but-gated (O-4), never presented as live or MVP.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: eval-stages-named\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"RUNBOOK.md names the deterministic PR-gate tier, the manual/nightly live tier reporting pass@k and pass^k separately, the `--pressure` probe whose transcripts must be read by a human, and the three demo modes with banner semantics — consistent with ADR-007 and ADR-017.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: checkpoint-rule-documented\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"Per decision-checkpoint-referent option (a): RUNBOOK.md/README.md state that the pinned account model (config/settings.py CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL) cannot resume a checkpoint produced by another model and that per-model cache minimums are re-verified on model upgrades (ADR-006). If the owner selects another referent this criterion changes.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: release-note-type-correct\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"Per decision-release-note-type: the new releases/_next note's `**Type:**` matches the highest v1.2.0 path class of the files actually changed — `minor` if any behaviour path (run.py/demo.py) is edited (option a), `patch` if only docs are edited (option b).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - id: no-authority-doc-edits\\\\n    criterion: \\\\\\\"docs/architecture.md and docs/decisions.md are unchanged; the reconciliation adds no behaviour claim beyond what those ADRs state.\\\\\\\"\\\\nout_of_scope:\\\\n  - item: \\\\\\\"Editing docs/architecture.md or docs/decisions.md, or adding a superseding ADR (the append-only authority; internal drift is a GAP, not an edit target here).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - item: \\\\\\\"Any contract version bump, re-pin, or edit to contract/PINNED.json or tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - item: \\\\\\\"Any change to config/settings.py, harness/claude_account_cli.py, harness/agent.py or provider-selection/eval mechanics (behaviour).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - item: \\\\\\\"Running the live tier or any network/credentialed run; a docs-only change needs none.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - item: \\\\\\\"Editing harness/usage.py report help text or tests/unit/test_usage.py (not planned).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - item: \\\\\\\"Redesigning the run.py/demo.py CLI surface or the evaluation tiers beyond reconciling their descriptive prose.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\"}\"}","structured_output":{"tool_name":"final","arguments_json":"{\"response\":\"contract_version: 0.1.0\\nartifact_version: 1\\nwork_item: 20260908T113253\\nobservable_behaviour:\\n  - id: readme-reflects-provider\\n    behaviour: \\\"README.md names `claude_account` (Claude CLI, subscription OAuth, model `claude-sonnet-4-6`) as the default provider per ADR-019 and `anthropic_sdk` as an explicit, potentially-metered opt-in; no statement claims the Anthropic SDK is the default and nothing leads with a stale provider/auth description drawn from architecture.md §8/§9.\\\"\\n  - id: readme-reflects-pipeline\\n    behaviour: \\\"README.md summarises the implemented M1–M5 pipeline status honestly: the server layer is carried but unwired (O-2) and forecasting (VC-POC-14) is registered-but-gated (O-4), not part of MVP.\\\"\\n  - id: runbook-reflects-stages\\n    behaviour: \\\"RUNBOOK.md names, in current terms, the deterministic PR-gate tier (pytest, zero network), the manual/nightly live tier (`python -m evals.live`) reporting pass@k and pass^k separately, the `--pressure` probe whose transcripts a human must read, the three demo modes and banner semantics, and the provider override (`HARNESS_MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic_sdk`, potentially metered).\\\"\\n  - id: release-note-present\\n    behaviour: \\\"Exactly one new releases/_next/<slug>.md exists carrying a `**Type:**` line and the mandatory `## Local deployment`, `## Manual steps` and `## Verification` (with a fenced bash block) sections, so the release-notes CI gate accepts the change; VERSION is untouched and no releases/v*.md is added.\\\"\\n  - id: no-behaviour-change\\n    behaviour: \\\"run.py and demo.py change only help text, argparse `description`/`help=` and docstrings/comments where they name provider/model or eval stages; no runtime logic, exit code, control-flow or symbol behaviour changes.\\\"\\nrequired_outputs:\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: README.md\\n    reason: \\\"The primary lagging surface: its top-level provider/model, evaluation-tier and pipeline-status prose must be reconciled to ADR-019, O-2 and O-4.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: RUNBOOK.md\\n    reason: \\\"The request names runbook guidance as a reconciliation target; operator prose for auth, the two eval tiers, --pressure, demo modes, provider override and the pin/checkpoint rules must be confirmed/tightened in current terms.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: releases/_next/reconcile-doc-surfaces.md\\n    reason: \\\"The release-notes CI gate (.github/workflows/pr-checks.yml release-notes job + .claude/hooks/require-release-notes.sh) requires exactly one new releases/_next/*.md with a Type line and the mandatory sections; the PR is blocked without it. Executor must use this slug.\\\"\\npermitted_files:\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: run.py\\n    reason: \\\"Help/description/docstring may be edited where it names provider/model or eval stages; contingent and no-logic per the plan. Editing it makes the change span a behaviour path (see decision-release-note-type).\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: demo.py\\n    reason: \\\"Mode/help/docstring prose may be aligned to ADR-017's three modes and banner semantics; contingent and no-logic. Must not add a `def render_*` or a second verbosity control (test_demo.py).\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_run_cli.py\\n    reason: \\\"Enforcing file over run.py: it greps run.py source and asserts the require_credentials message strings. Editable only if a require_credentials message string is deliberately changed, in which case its paired assertions must move in lockstep.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_demo.py\\n    reason: \\\"Enforcing file over demo.py: it asserts ADR-017 properties (no `def render_*`, renders through cli.render_text, GROUPS/GATED partition, single LOG_LEVEL setdefault, no setLevel) and may gain/adjust an assertion over edited mode/help text.\\\"\\ndeterministic:\\n  - id: full-test-suite\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The declared verification suite (manifest k-12Harness.verify) exits zero with no failures and no errors; pre-existing xfail/xpass are unaffected.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\n  - id: demo-properties-green\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_demo.py -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The ADR-017 property tests over demo.py stay green after the help/docstring edits (no def render_*, renders through run.py, groups partition, single verbosity control).\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\n  - id: run-cli-green\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_run_cli.py -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The CLI tests, including the require_credentials message and default_credentials source assertions, stay green after any run.py help edits.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\n  - id: contract-pin-unchanged\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The contract pin test stays green, proving no accidental contract/PINNED.json or CONTRACT_VERSION change (ADR-008); this is a docs-only WI with no contract bump.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ (failed|error)'\\n  - id: release-note-typed\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\"grep -RE '^\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\*Type:\\\\\\\\*\\\\\\\\* (patch|minor|major)' releases/_next/\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The added releases/_next/ note declares a patch|minor|major Type line, as the release-notes gate requires; the base commit carries only releases/_next/.gitkeep, so exit 0 here depends on the change.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\nmust_not_change:\\n  - invariant: \\\"The require_credentials message strings in run.py asserted by tests/unit/test_run_cli.py (`claude setup-token`, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`, and the `default_credentials` source reference) — kept intact, or their paired assertions updated in the same change.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"ADR-017 properties of demo.py: no `def render_*`, every answer renders via `cli.render_text(output)`, `demo.GROUPS`/`demo.GATED` partition the registry, and the single `os.environ.setdefault(\\\\\\\"LOG_LEVEL\\\\\\\", ...)` control point with no direct `setLevel` (tests/unit/test_demo.py).\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"Runtime behaviour of run.py and demo.py: no logic, exit code, argument parsing semantics or symbol behaviour change — only help/description/docstring/comment prose.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"contract/PINNED.json, tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py and settings.CONTRACT_VERSION: no contract version bump or re-pin in this WI.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"VERSION is not touched and no releases/v*.md is added (the release-notes gate refuses both); exactly one releases/_next/*.md is added.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"docs/architecture.md and docs/decisions.md (the pinned authority) are not edited; config/settings.py and the provider adapters (harness/claude_account_cli.py, harness/agent.py) carry no change.\\\"\\nfailure_behaviour:\\n  - condition: \\\"A require_credentials message string in run.py is changed without updating tests/unit/test_run_cli.py.\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"test_run_cli.py fails; the executor must either keep the message strings intact or update the paired assertions in the same change.\\\"\\n  - condition: \\\"demo.py grows a `def render_*`, stops rendering through `cli.render_text`, or adds a second verbosity control.\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"tests/unit/test_demo.py fails; the demo must continue to render through run.py and keep the single LOG_LEVEL control.\\\"\\n  - condition: \\\"VERSION is bumped, a releases/v*.md is added, no releases/_next/*.md is added, more than one is added, or the note lacks the Type line or a mandatory section.\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The release-notes CI gate and the local require-release-notes.sh hook deny the PR with an actionable reason; the change is blocked until the note conforms.\\\"\\ncompatibility:\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-019: `claude_account` (Claude CLI, subscription OAuth, `claude-sonnet-4-6`) is the default provider and `anthropic_sdk` is explicit-and-potentially-metered; ADR-018 (Codex account) remains as history, superseded by ADR-019 — doc prose must state this and add no new superseding ADR.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-007: the live tier stays manual/nightly and never becomes a PR gate; the deterministic tier gates every PR at zero network cost.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-017: the demo has exactly three modes each announced by a tested banner and renders only through the product; doc prose must not contradict this.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-008 / ADR-015-3: the contract is pinned by hash and a bump is the loud four-step operation (re-pin, regenerate the prompt, regenerate the fixture bundle, re-point cases); the Anthropic SDK is pinned exactly alongside the framework as one compatibility surface — documented, not performed here.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-006: per-model cache minimums (CACHE_MIN_TOKENS) are re-verified on model upgrades and the cache regression check remains `cache_read_tokens > 0`.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"README.md's own precedence rule stands: docs/decisions.md is the source of truth on any conflict, so where architecture.md §8/§9 disagree with ADR-019 the surfaces adopt ADR-019.\\\"\\ncompatibility_baselines: []\\ncontract_requirements:\\n  - id: scope-is-the-file-list\\n    requirement: \\\"The permitted change set is exactly required_outputs plus permitted_files. docs/architecture.md, docs/decisions.md, config/settings.py, the provider adapters, contract/PINNED.json, tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py, tests/unit/test_usage.py and harness/usage.py are outside scope.\\\"\\n  - id: decision-checkpoint-referent\\n    requirement: \\\"DECISION: which 'checkpoint compatibility rules' referent the doc surfaces reconcile to. Options: (a) the model-checkpoint/resume rule — the pinned account model (config/settings.py CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL) cannot resume a checkpoint produced by another model, per-model cache minimums re-verified on upgrade (ADR-006); (b) the eval-resume checkpoint (RUNBOOK §1 `--resume`); (c) the contract hash pin (ADR-008); (d) the SDK+framework pin surface (ADR-015-3). Neither Definition Pack reference defines a 'checkpoint' concept, so this is an owner choice. The rest of the contract is written on option (a). Affects: semantic checkpoint-rule-documented, observable_behaviour runbook-reflects-stages, and RUNBOOK.md / README.md content in required_outputs.\\\"\\n  - id: decision-release-note-type\\n    requirement: \\\"DECISION: whether the reconciliation edits the code entry points (run.py, demo.py) at all. Under the v1.2.0 path classes, any change to a root *.py behaviour path makes the release note `**Type:** minor`; a docs-only change (README, RUNBOOK, the note) is `**Type:** patch`. Options: (a) edit run.py/demo.py help/docstrings where they name provider/model/eval stages — release note Type: minor, run.py and demo.py are in the change set; (b) leave run.py/demo.py untouched — release note Type: patch. The contract is written on option (a) (the plan lists run.py/demo.py as in-scope surfaces) but keeps them in permitted_files so option (b) needs no restructuring; the release-note-typed deterministic accepts either Type. Affects: permitted_files (run.py, demo.py), observable_behaviour no-behaviour-change, semantic release-note-type-correct, deterministic release-note-typed.\\\"\\n  - id: gap-architecture-adr-conflict\\n    requirement: \\\"GAP: docs/architecture.md §8 (names the model plainly) and §9 (API-key/account-bearer auth) predate and conflict with docs/decisions.md ADR-018/019. Resolved by the repository's stated precedence (README.md: decisions.md is source of truth on any conflict): the surfaces adopt ADR-019; architecture.md is not edited here (its internal drift is out of scope).\\\"\\n  - id: assumption-readme-primary\\n    requirement: \\\"ASSUMPTION: README.md is the primary lagging surface; run.py, demo.py and RUNBOOK.md already largely reflect ADR-019, so reconciliation there is confirmation/tightening. The executor should diff each surface against the two pinned ADR sets before editing.\\\"\\n  - id: assumption-model-literal-source\\n    requirement: \\\"ASSUMPTION: the implemented pipeline/provider reality lives partly in code the manifest did not pin (config/settings.py, run.py, harness/claude_account_cli.py); where prose must name the pinned model it should point at config/settings.py as the single source of truth rather than restating a literal that can drift.\\\"\\nsemantic:\\n  - id: provider-default-adopts-adr019\\n    criterion: \\\"README.md and RUNBOOK.md describe `claude_account` (Claude CLI, subscription OAuth, `claude-sonnet-4-6`) as the default provider and `anthropic_sdk` as explicit/potentially-metered, with no residual claim that the Anthropic SDK is the default and no stale auth description contradicting ADR-019.\\\"\\n  - id: pipeline-status-honest\\n    criterion: \\\"README.md's pipeline summary states the M1–M5 reality without overstating it: the server layer is carried but unwired (O-2) and forecasting is registered-but-gated (O-4), never presented as live or MVP.\\\"\\n  - id: eval-stages-named\\n    criterion: \\\"RUNBOOK.md names the deterministic PR-gate tier, the manual/nightly live tier reporting pass@k and pass^k separately, the `--pressure` probe whose transcripts must be read by a human, and the three demo modes with banner semantics — consistent with ADR-007 and ADR-017.\\\"\\n  - id: checkpoint-rule-documented\\n    criterion: \\\"Per decision-checkpoint-referent option (a): RUNBOOK.md/README.md state that the pinned account model (config/settings.py CLAUDE_ACCOUNT_MODEL) cannot resume a checkpoint produced by another model and that per-model cache minimums are re-verified on model upgrades (ADR-006). If the owner selects another referent this criterion changes.\\\"\\n  - id: release-note-type-correct\\n    criterion: \\\"Per decision-release-note-type: the new releases/_next note's `**Type:**` matches the highest v1.2.0 path class of the files actually changed — `minor` if any behaviour path (run.py/demo.py) is edited (option a), `patch` if only docs are edited (option b).\\\"\\n  - id: no-authority-doc-edits\\n    criterion: \\\"docs/architecture.md and docs/decisions.md are unchanged; the reconciliation adds no behaviour claim beyond what those ADRs state.\\\"\\nout_of_scope:\\n  - item: \\\"Editing docs/architecture.md or docs/decisions.md, or adding a superseding ADR (the append-only authority; internal drift is a GAP, not an edit target here).\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Any contract version bump, re-pin, or edit to contract/PINNED.json or tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py.\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Any change to config/settings.py, harness/claude_account_cli.py, harness/agent.py or provider-selection/eval mechanics (behaviour).\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Running the live tier or any network/credentialed run; a docs-only change needs none.\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Editing harness/usage.py report help text or tests/unit/test_usage.py (not planned).\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Redesigning the run.py/demo.py CLI surface or the evaluation tiers beyond reconciling their descriptive prose.\\\"\\n\"}"},"ttft_ms":144961,"type":"result","duration_ms":207404,"uuid":"f6f0712f-f763-443b-bb20-de7e909fc8ff","ttft_stream_ms":3358,"time_to_request_ms":545,"first_content_frame_ms":3358,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
